{
  "id": 470475861,
  "iid": 24182,
  "project_id": 7898047,
  "title": "SMB: Improve wc and index description of SMB1 NEGOTIATE response",
  "description": "Wireshark dissector for SMB1 dialects in NEGOTIATE response has logic: Guessed dialect type (e.g. \"Greater than CORE PROTOCOL and up to LANMAN2.1\") is based on the word count field (wc) and the real selected dialect (e.g. \"DOS LM1.2X002\") is from the followup 16-bit index number after the word count which belongs to the index string found in NEGOTIATE request. Note that request packet does not have to be available (if is not captured) and in this case the real selected dialect is unknown for dissector.\n\nImprove displaying description for the guessed dialect and the real selected dialect. Put the guessed dialect string into the \"Word Count\" field and the real selected dialect string into the \"Selected Index\" field. So this will match the dissector logic.\n\nBefore this change the NEGOTIATE response packet had this:\n\n```\nWord Count (WCT): 13\nSelected Index: 2, Greater than CORE PROTOCOL and up to LANMAN2.1\n```\n\nAfter this change the NEGOTIATE response packet has this:\n\n```\nWord Count (WCT): 13 (Greater than CORE PROTOCOL and up to LANMAN2.1)\nSelected Index: 2 (DOS LM1.2X002)\n```",
  "state": "merged",
  "created_at": "2026-04-03T23:07:07.020Z",
  "updated_at": "2026-04-10T15:32:15.755Z",
